Official API/KAT files
----------------------

Each software C implementation leaf directory contains the official API/KAT
file set:

~~~text
CryptHash_AlgorithmInstance.c
CryptHash_AlgorithmInstance.h
KAT_CryptHash.c
drng.c
drng.h
~~~

KAT_CryptHash.c, drng.c, and drng.h are copied unchanged from the official API
package and are not modified. CryptHash_AlgorithmInstance.c and
CryptHash_AlgorithmInstance.h keep the official CryptHash() interface and set
the instance-specific ALGORITHM_INSTANCE and DIGEST_BIT_LENGTH values.

Build and run
-------------

Below is the command for the "Reference implementation". To run other implementations, the word "reference" in each command should be replaced by other names following the "Implementation options" section.

~~~sh
cd <package-root>
mkdir -p build/reference
cd build/reference
cmake \
  -DMCUBE_IMPL=reference \
  ../../Implementations
make
make run
~~~

To set a specific C compiler, pass it to cmake (the project is C-only;
`CC=` environment variables are ignored once CMakeCache.txt exists):

~~~sh
cmake \
  -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=gcc \
  -DMCUBE_IMPL=reference \
  ../../Implementations
~~~

make builds one `kat_crypthash` KAT executable per digest size, each in its
own subdirectory under the build tree:

~~~text
build/reference/MasterCube-512/kat_crypthash
build/reference/MasterCube-768/kat_crypthash
build/reference/MasterCube-1024/kat_crypthash
~~~

make run and make verify do the same thing: build and run each instance's
kat_crypthash, then diff the generated KAT output files against the reference
copies in Test_Vectors/. If any file is missing or mismatched, the command
reports an error and exits non-zero.

Run verification:

~~~sh
cd <package-root>/build/reference
make verify
~~~

If "make verify" ends without any error, it means the implementations works as expected.

Implementation options
----------------------

Use the same command pattern as above and replace reference with one of:

~~~text
x86-performance
x86-resource
x86-avx512
arm-resource
arm-performance
~~~

Compiler options selected by CMake:

~~~text
reference       -std=c99 -Wpedantic -Wall -Wextra -O2
x86-performance -O3 -march=x86-64 -mavx2 -mtune=native -flto -fomit-frame-pointer -std=c99 -Wpedantic -Wall -Wextra
x86-resource    -Os -march=x86-64 -mavx2 -flto -fomit-frame-pointer -std=c99 -Wpedantic -Wall -Wextra
x86-avx512      -O3 -march=x86-64 -mavx512f -mavx512bw -mavx512vl -mtune=native -flto -fomit-frame-pointer -std=c99 -Wpedantic -Wall -Wextra
arm-resource    -Os -march=armv8-a -flto -fomit-frame-pointer -std=c99 -Wpedantic -Wall -Wextra
arm-performance -O3 -march=<auto> -flto -fomit-frame-pointer -std=c99 -Wpedantic -Wall -Wextra
~~~

For arm-performance, <auto> selects armv8.2-a+sve on ARM hosts with SVE support
and armv8.2-a on ARMv8.2 hosts without SVE. It can be overridden with
-DMCUBE_ARM_PERFORMANCE_MARCH=armv8.2-a+sve or
-DMCUBE_ARM_PERFORMANCE_MARCH=armv8.2-a.

Custom implementation directory:

~~~sh
cd <package-root>
mkdir -p build/custom
cd build/custom
cmake \
  -DMCUBE_IMPLDIR=<relative-implementation-path> \
  ../../Implementations
make
make run
~~~
